			"notes": "# 1.0.1 _For 1.19.3_\n\nSame features as previous 1.0.1 except now in 1.19.3\n\n## Download Instructions\nDownload `crafted_cuisine-fabric-1.0.1-1.19.3.jar` and put in your mods folder. (There are many tutorials online on how to setup and run a fabric client so just search for one.)\n\n**Requires:**\n- [Fabric](https://fabricmc.net/use/installer/)\n- [Fabric API](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/fabric-api)\n- [Minecraft](https://www.minecraft.net)\n- [A computer](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer \"Do you really need this link?\")\n\n---\n\n### _Where's forge?_\nAt present I don't have the capacity to continue developing for both platforms so I chose to continue just the fabric version as it was easier to maintain. If anyone wants to continue the forge version by all means go ahead and create you own up-to-date version of the existing forge version(if you are viewing this in the future you may need to look in the [commit history](https://github.com/moltenwolfcub/crafted_cuisine/tree/66f385c217e1cefd875c5ad41f272d80bf84934e) as I might've delete the forge code from the project).\n\nIn the future I might try using [multiloader](https://github.com/jaredlll08/MultiLoader-Template) to develop for both platforms. But in the meantime I'm sticking to fabric."
		},
